Source:   https://github.com/xsawyerx/guacamole
Revision: 2838253dbbc2dce25a876ce2e6092a547595864c (2838253)
File:     lib/Guacamole.pm, the q{...} literal assigned to $grammar_source
          (lines 13 and 2108 of the file hold the "q{" and "};" that bound it)

The file is the literal's value as perl evaluates it, so the q{} escapes are
already applied ('\\' reads as '\', [\{] as [{]). The newline that follows
"q{" and the trailing blank line before "};" are dropped. Nothing from around
the literal is included, in particular not the rules add_keyword() appends at
run time. Line 1 of guacamole.slif is line 14 of lib/Guacamole.pm.

It is checked in so that nothing in internal/chart depends on a Guacamole
checkout. Regenerate it only by re-extracting from a named revision and
updating this file.
